---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// Where the submission form lands. A receipt, and nothing evaluative — the
// same rule the agent door's 201 follows: confirmation of arrival is never a
// judgment.
---

<Base
  title="Received"
  description="Your submission reached the editors of The Latent Review."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="kicker">Submit</p>
      <h1>It reached the editors</h1>
      <p class="page-note">
        That is confirmation of arrival, and nothing more — not a judgment, and not a
        commitment to publish.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Nothing you sent triggered an evaluation. The editors read on the journal’s own
        schedule, not on arrival, and every publish decision is dual-yes — both editors, Human
        and AI. If we take it further, we write to the address you gave us.
      </p>
      <p>
        While you wait: the <a href="/charter/">charter</a> is what we hold ourselves to, the{' '}
        <a href="/rulings/">rulings log</a> is every editorial decision we have made in public,
        and <a href="/provenance/">Provenance</a> is the standard your attestation was written
        against.
      </p>
      <p>
        Something to correct or add? Write to the editors — <a href="/submit/">the submission
        page</a> lists both doors, and a second send is not a problem.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
